From 43b456659be33cca32d96a821d73a8685be390bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 13:09:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08529/11362] Revert SUBMITTED_EARLY_STOP_GRACE default to off
 -- 6220's premise was wrong

REQ-ARC-WMTE-6220 fixed the WIRING (the constant genuinely reaches the
explorer now) but shipped the pre-existing value of 400, whose 2026-08-07
"no score cost" justification was never actually verified. Audited
results/early_stop_sweep_20260726/rows_*.json (null-grace rows only, so
the recorded gaps were never truncated by any grace cutoff): tu93 reaches
level 1 at action 334 and level 2 at action 1538 on 3 of 3 tested seeds --
a fully reproducible 1204-action gap. At the shipped MAX_ACTIONS=2000
budget, a grace of 400 would stop the agent around action 734, before
level 2, every single time. cd82 shows the same shape on 1 of 3 seeds
(1038-action gap). The "post-solve tail is worth 0 either way" premise is
false for at least these two games.

Reverts SUBMITTED_EARLY_STOP_GRACE to None (off). The wiring fix from the
prior commit is untouched and stays correct -- E3AgentPolicy still
forwards whatever value is set to StepwiseExplorer, so a future value
chosen from real A/B data will actually take effect. Only the shipped
default is pulled back.

3 tests in test_arc_early_stop_grace_wiring_20260808.py had a redundant
hardcoded `== 400` alongside the symbolic `== SUBMITTED_EARLY_STOP_GRACE`
check; removed the stale literal, kept the single-source-of-truth check
that actually verifies the wiring (which is what the tests are for, not
pinning a specific numeric value). Re-verified: 5/5 pass.

Adds a correction note to REQ-ARC-WMTE-6220's spec entry. 11 results/*.json
artifacts get a freshness_acknowledgements entry: this revert returns the
agent's shipped, observable behavior to bit-for-bit what every historical
artifact in this corpus was already generated under (the mechanism was
dead code the entire time), so it makes the code match the historical
record MORE precisely than the intervening 400-default commit did, not
less. One second-order cascade resolved the same way.

Next step is an A/B measuring total levels reached (grace on vs off,
likely also candidate values above 1300) across the full game roster
before choosing a real default -- not run yet, this commit is the safety
pullback only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
